      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "As of January, the Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services began paying for chronic care management of patients with two or more conditions under its Chronic Care Management program. The payment applies to patients in traditional fee-for-service and noncapitated Medicare Advantage plan arrangements. Texas Medical Association leaders caution the program has some hefty requirements."},
